# Print link

The publishing print control either invokes the browser print dialog or links to an existing print view. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/print-link/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Printing can help with offline recovery guidance, maintenance notes and a household quick reference. Include the page title, revision and meaningful text in the print output. A chart printout also needs its unit, selected period and data alternative.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a button for a browser action and a real link for a separate printable page. Hide action controls and decorative navigation in print styles while preserving warnings and content. For a multi-part guide, assemble a complete print view before offering a link to it.

## Home Assistant boundary

Both examples invoke window.print() only when the person selects Print this example. This opens the browser print dialog for the isolated example document. The action controls are omitted from print output, while the example content remains. No PDF is generated or uploaded, and opening the dialog does not claim a successful print. Without JavaScript, use the browser’s own Print command; the example button remains disabled. Test the real print preview, including expanded and collapsed history.

